1
00:00:00,528 --> 00:00:03,150
Announcer thing, Announcer
thing, Announcer thing!

2
00:00:03,150 --> 00:00:03,530
What?

3
00:00:03,530 --> 00:00:06,430
You know how we were having
trouble with the jigsaw puzzle?

4
00:00:06,430 --> 00:00:06,770
Yeah?

5
00:00:06,770 --> 00:00:09,730
Well, we solved it, and so we're free!

6
00:00:09,730 --> 00:00:10,711
That's good to know.

7
00:00:11,093 --> 00:00:14,631
Did you know I've never been
voted for to be eliminated?

8
00:00:14,835 --> 00:00:16,230
Wow! Coolio!

9
00:00:16,230 --> 00:00:19,270
I'm the only Squishy Cherry who's like that.

10
00:00:19,270 --> 00:00:22,580
The only other people who haven't been voted for are

11
00:00:22,580 --> 00:00:23,150
Leafy,

12
00:00:23,150 --> 00:00:23,760
Teardrop,

13
00:00:23,760 --> 00:00:25,100
Rocky, and...

14
00:00:25,100 --> 00:00:25,760
Snowball!

15
00:00:25,760 --> 00:00:29,013
Crudliously? Snowball's never been voted for?

16
00:00:29,146 --> 00:00:30,250
But he's a jerk.

17
00:00:30,250 --> 00:00:31,880
Yeah, well, you know...

18
00:00:31,880 --> 00:00:34,844
Oh! You know, I've been voted for in four episodes.

19
00:00:35,155 --> 00:00:36,480
No one else has been.

20
00:00:36,480 --> 00:00:39,937
Well, that's okay because you're still here!

21
00:00:40,337 --> 00:00:42,110
Now for my vote status!

22
00:00:42,110 --> 00:00:42,420
I-

23
00:00:42,420 --> 00:00:45,330
I've only been voted once, by Artofliving123,

24
00:00:45,330 --> 00:00:46,650
even though I shouldn't have been.

25
00:00:46,650 --> 00:00:48,030
Really, Bubble?

26
00:00:48,030 --> 00:00:50,702
You know, I think your voice has changed.

27
00:00:50,915 --> 00:00:52,880
WAAAH! You're not Bubble!

28
00:00:52,880 --> 00:00:53,890
No, I'm not.

29
00:00:53,890 --> 00:00:55,297
You murdered her!

30
00:00:55,297 --> 00:00:57,290
Yeah, well, that is true.

31
00:00:57,493 --> 00:01:04,186
♪ [INTRO PLAYS] ♪

32
00:01:04,186 --> 00:01:06,186
Subtitles: Daniel Adam Valle

33
00:01:06,791 --> 00:01:10,080
Anyway, since there was no voting
last time, there is no Cake at Stake.

34
00:01:10,080 --> 00:01:11,866
So, we can get right to the contest.

35
00:01:12,160 --> 00:01:12,970
It's a relay race.

36
00:01:12,970 --> 00:01:13,437
- STUMP!

37
00:01:13,437 --> 00:01:14,062
- OW!
- STUMP!

38
00:01:14,133 --> 00:01:16,462
Hold on a second! There's something that's unfair!

39
00:01:16,577 --> 00:01:19,270
My team has many more members than the other team.

40
00:01:19,270 --> 00:01:22,520
So, if everyone goes once, we'll take much LONGER!

41
00:01:22,520 --> 00:01:23,750
OK, I'll fix that.

42
00:01:23,750 --> 00:01:25,960
Four people of the Cherry team will go twice.

43
00:01:25,960 --> 00:01:29,635
Not fair! We'll TIRE by the second time through!

44
00:01:29,733 --> 00:01:31,390
Well then, no one goes twice,

45
00:01:31,390 --> 00:01:34,990
but on the Grapes, only five of the
people go, so four people don't go.

46
00:01:34,990 --> 00:01:40,222
Not fair! THEY get to choose
the best players but WE can't!

47
00:01:40,302 --> 00:01:42,364
Grr. Then what do you suggest the rules to be?

48
00:01:42,462 --> 00:01:43,777
How about this?

49
00:01:43,866 --> 00:01:46,960
Like you just said, five on each team go,

50
00:01:46,960 --> 00:01:51,662
but YOU randomly choose which
five Grapes participate in the race!

51
00:01:51,662 --> 00:01:53,660
Hm, I guess that sounds fair enough to me.

52
00:01:53,928 --> 00:01:55,800
Grapes, here's a nine-slice wheel.

53
00:01:55,800 --> 00:01:57,440
Each person has one slice.

54
00:01:57,440 --> 00:02:00,515
The first five people chosen by
this wheel participate in the race.

55
00:02:00,764 --> 00:02:02,300
So, someone give it a whirl.

56
00:02:02,300 --> 00:02:06,180
Since I'm the strongest one here by FAAAR,

57
00:02:06,180 --> 00:02:08,497
it better land on ME!

58
00:02:14,140 --> 00:02:16,657
Hi, weirdos! Here's another prank.

59
00:02:16,791 --> 00:02:19,262
But this one involves Ice Cube instead of Bubble.

60
00:02:19,466 --> 00:02:21,680
Just take an Ice Cube Recovery Center and, like,

61
00:02:21,680 --> 00:02:24,275
just carry it over to the edge of a cliff...

62
00:02:24,382 --> 00:02:26,320
maybe...with a tree...

63
00:02:26,320 --> 00:02:28,200
Yeah, yeah. With a tree. Definitely, yeah.

64
00:02:28,200 --> 00:02:29,230
That's mandatory.

65
00:02:29,230 --> 00:02:34,044
And attach a spring from the tree
to the Ice Cube Recovery Center,

66
00:02:34,088 --> 00:02:37,480
and then...melt...Ice Cube.

67
00:02:37,480 --> 00:02:38,650
[WHISPERING]
Melting her kills her, right?

68
00:02:38,650 --> 00:02:39,200
???
Yeaaah.

69
00:02:39,200 --> 00:02:40,071
BLOCKY
Okay, good.

70
00:02:40,133 --> 00:02:43,928
[NORMAL] Ice Cube is recreated
in the Ice Cube Recovery Center.

71
00:02:44,071 --> 00:02:46,490
She'll, like, weigh it down, and...

72
00:02:46,490 --> 00:02:49,180
the Ice Cube Recovery Center
will tilt down off the cliff,

73
00:02:49,180 --> 00:02:53,500
and Ice Cube will fall out, and she'll...
crash at the bottom of the...cliff!

74
00:02:53,500 --> 00:02:57,680
And Ice Cube is recreated in
the Ice Cube Recovery Center.

75
00:02:57,680 --> 00:03:03,120
She'll, like, weigh it down, and the Ice Cube
Recovery Center will tilt down off the cliff.

76
00:03:03,120 --> 00:03:04,311
Cycle repeats!

77
00:03:04,568 --> 00:03:05,893
Yeah, isn't that cool?

78
00:03:06,133 --> 00:03:07,040
Pretty funny?

79
00:03:07,306 --> 00:03:13,884
This program was brought to you
by Blocky's Funny Doings International.

80
00:03:18,888 --> 00:03:19,973
Oh, no.

81
00:03:20,142 --> 00:03:22,417
You'd BETTER be a good runner!

82
00:03:22,560 --> 00:03:23,270
Are you?

83
00:03:23,270 --> 00:03:25,102
Yeah, WATCH! Here we go.

84
00:03:27,777 --> 00:03:29,991
Wow, you're such a fast runner!

85
00:03:29,991 --> 00:03:31,990
Thank you, wise Ice Cube!

86
00:03:31,990 --> 00:03:34,510
Wow, you're such a slow runner!

87
00:03:34,510 --> 00:03:36,782
No thank you, dumb Coiny!

88
00:03:37,555 --> 00:03:38,257
Spin again.

89
00:03:43,724 --> 00:03:44,373
Bleh!

90
00:03:47,200 --> 00:03:49,620
Um, who's on that slice?

91
00:03:49,620 --> 00:03:51,875
I ain't scraping that off!

92
00:03:51,946 --> 00:03:53,730
Well, process of elimination!

93
00:03:53,730 --> 00:03:56,490
There's SB, Leafy, Rocky, me,

94
00:03:56,490 --> 00:03:58,430
Teardrop, Tennis Ball, and Coiny.

95
00:03:58,430 --> 00:04:00,620
Firey's been chosen, so it's Ice Cube!

96
00:04:00,620 --> 00:04:03,884
Oh, great. A weak, ARMLESS one.

97
00:04:05,457 --> 00:04:09,422
Ha-ha, HA! Oh, that's just great! A-ha!

98
00:04:12,942 --> 00:04:13,848
Two spots left.

99
00:04:16,613 --> 00:04:18,990
There's only one more person
participating in this race.

100
00:04:18,990 --> 00:04:22,311
If it isn't ME, we are DEAD!

101
00:04:24,568 --> 00:04:25,271
NOOOOOOOOOOOOO!

102
00:04:25,271 --> 00:04:28,124
[SPED UP]
NOOOOOOOOOOOOO!

103
00:04:28,382 --> 00:04:31,066
Ha-ha! You didn't make the team!

104
00:04:31,333 --> 00:04:31,955
OW!

105
00:04:32,160 --> 00:04:34,231
So, yes. You five will compete.

106
00:04:34,337 --> 00:04:35,540
You four won't.

107
00:04:35,540 --> 00:04:36,990
So, the rules are simple.

108
00:04:36,990 --> 00:04:38,520
Just run to the tree and back.

109
00:04:38,520 --> 00:04:41,950
Oh! Also, in this episode,
no one's getting sent to the TLC.

110
00:04:41,950 --> 00:04:44,328
Again, for, like, the second time?

111
00:04:44,400 --> 00:04:46,533
I liked it when there was elimination.

112
00:04:46,595 --> 00:04:49,600
It adds anticipation and self-preservation!

113
00:04:49,600 --> 00:04:52,560
Don't worry. Next episode,
two people will be eliminated.

114
00:04:52,560 --> 00:04:53,950
But I'll get to that later.

115
00:04:53,950 --> 00:04:57,020
So, nothing happens to the losers.
The winners get a prize.

116
00:04:57,020 --> 00:04:58,610
Which IS...?

117
00:04:58,610 --> 00:04:59,550
You'll find out later.

118
00:04:59,550 --> 00:05:00,820
GRRRRRRR!

119
00:05:00,820 --> 00:05:01,860
But there is one catch.

120
00:05:01,860 --> 00:05:04,755
While running, you must carry
the person who will run the race after you.

121
00:05:04,915 --> 00:05:07,040
The last person in line doesn't carry anyone.

122
00:05:07,146 --> 00:05:09,510
Yeah! I don't have to carry anyone!

123
00:05:09,510 --> 00:05:11,760
Yeah! I only have to carry Bubble!

124
00:05:11,760 --> 00:05:15,964
I have to carry Match, and
I know she's gaining weight!

125
00:05:16,460 --> 00:05:16,812
ANNOUNCER: Go.

126
00:05:16,812 --> 00:05:19,102
Faster, Eraser faster!

127
00:05:19,644 --> 00:05:21,800
- AAAWAAAAHHH!
- Why are you screaming, Ice Cube?

128
00:05:21,800 --> 00:05:23,191
- AAAWAAAAHHH!
- Are you melting?

129
00:05:24,930 --> 00:05:26,506
Get on, Pencil!

130
00:05:26,675 --> 00:05:28,700
She's pretty much gone.

131
00:05:28,700 --> 00:05:32,350
The Ice Cube Recovery Center won't
start until she's completely melted!

132
00:05:32,350 --> 00:05:34,640
Well, what are you waiting for? Melt, Firey!

133
00:05:36,888 --> 00:05:38,408
Here comes the tree!

134
00:05:39,448 --> 00:05:43,253
Icy, because you have no arms, I'll have to sit on you.

135
00:05:43,315 --> 00:05:44,330
Go, go, go!

136
00:05:44,330 --> 00:05:45,697
We're here!

137
00:05:46,290 --> 00:05:48,951
AAAAAAHHHHH!

138
00:05:49,875 --> 00:05:52,150
Pencil, I'm not fat, am I?

139
00:05:52,150 --> 00:05:54,960
I was just JK kidding, Match!

140
00:05:54,960 --> 00:05:56,310
Oh, okay then.

141
00:05:56,310 --> 00:05:57,760
Back on!

142
00:05:57,760 --> 00:05:59,120
Hey, they lapped us!

143
00:05:59,235 --> 00:06:00,160
Release!

144
00:06:00,160 --> 00:06:01,390
Hey, Golf Ball.

145
00:06:01,390 --> 00:06:03,431
Oh, WOW, you're HEAVY!

146
00:06:03,813 --> 00:06:06,595
Match, not so hard! You'll pop me!

147
00:06:07,084 --> 00:06:09,422
Uh-oh! Where's the BRC?

148
00:06:19,900 --> 00:06:21,300
I'm coming, Match!

149
00:06:21,300 --> 00:06:23,580
Wow, you're HEAVY!

150
00:06:23,580 --> 00:06:25,422
You already said that!

151
00:06:25,475 --> 00:06:26,437
- BUBBLE: I'm getting there! Coming!

152
00:06:26,437 --> 00:06:27,521
- OMT, she'd better get here soon.
- BUBBLE: I'm getting there! Coming!

153
00:06:27,521 --> 00:06:29,354
- OMT, she'd better get here soon.
- BUBBLE: Almost there! A little bit more!

154
00:06:29,354 --> 00:06:30,060
- BUBBLE: Almost there! A little bit more!

155
00:06:30,060 --> 00:06:32,488
BUBBLE:
Where am I? I don't know where I am.

156
00:06:32,631 --> 00:06:33,431
Ugh!

157
00:06:33,928 --> 00:06:34,480
Hm!

158
00:06:34,960 --> 00:06:35,555
Bleh!

159
00:06:38,026 --> 00:06:40,400
Remember, Match: not too hard!

160
00:06:40,400 --> 00:06:41,857
O-kay!

161
00:06:46,600 --> 00:06:49,217
[GRAPES COMMAND]
Run, Rocky! RUN!

162
00:06:53,555 --> 00:06:54,240
Grr!

163
00:07:02,862 --> 00:07:04,271
[GRAPES COMMAND]
- Go, go!

164
00:07:04,271 --> 00:07:05,890
[GRAPES COMMAND]
- Run, Rocky! RUN!

165
00:07:05,890 --> 00:07:06,613
GRR!!!

166
00:07:08,826 --> 00:07:10,320
Yeah, we won!

167
00:07:10,320 --> 00:07:10,900
Yeah!

168
00:07:10,900 --> 00:07:12,950
We won? That's a relief.

169
00:07:12,950 --> 00:07:13,850
Yeah!

170
00:07:13,850 --> 00:07:18,213
I wasn't expecting we'd win, but I'm glad we DID!

171
00:07:18,346 --> 00:07:20,090
Thanks a lot, Bubble.

172
00:07:20,090 --> 00:07:22,533
It's your fault we lost!

173
00:07:22,853 --> 00:07:24,960
So, Grapes, do you want to know your prize?

174
00:07:24,960 --> 00:07:25,970
YEAAAH!

175
00:07:25,970 --> 00:07:27,900
You win an eliminated player onto your team.

176
00:07:27,900 --> 00:07:30,820
Uh, do we get to choose WHICH player?

177
00:07:30,820 --> 00:07:33,120
No, you do not. But voters, you do.

178
00:07:33,120 --> 00:07:35,520
You can vote an eliminated player back into the game.

179
00:07:35,520 --> 00:07:36,160
There's Flower-

180
00:07:36,160 --> 00:07:39,490
You'd BETTER vote me, or-or I'll CRUSH you!

181
00:07:39,490 --> 00:07:40,030
ANNOUNCER:
Spongy-

182
00:07:40,030 --> 00:07:41,900
Heeelllllooo.

183
00:07:41,900 --> 00:07:42,280
ANNOUNCER:
Blocky-

184
00:07:42,280 --> 00:07:45,413
Vote for me! I've got an edge!

185
00:07:45,422 --> 00:07:47,500
Well, twelve edges, actually.

186
00:07:47,500 --> 00:07:47,920
ANNOUNCER:
Woody-

187
00:07:47,920 --> 00:07:49,480
Ehhh....ahhh...

188
00:07:49,480 --> 00:07:49,820
ANNOUNCER:
Pin-

189
00:07:49,820 --> 00:07:51,760
You need a heroic leader like ME!

190
00:07:51,760 --> 00:07:52,550
ANNOUNCER:
and Needy.

191
00:07:52,550 --> 00:07:53,813
DON'T call me Needy!

192
00:08:02,450 --> 00:08:12,622
♪ [Kenet & Raz - Unreal Super Hero 3] ♪